	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Exception liée à un timestamp with timezone]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=13254#p13254"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Il semblerait que les dates soient gérées correctement jusqu&#039;au 01/05/1892 à 11h42, mais qu&#039;en dessous, cela provoque mon erreur :<br />&quot;1892-05-01 12:00:03+00&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 13:00:39+00&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 08:00:14+00:17:30&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 10:00:44+00:17:30&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 11:59:21+00&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 11:00:36+00:17:30&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 11:30:09+00:17:30&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 11:45:00+00&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 11:40:15+00:17:30&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 11:42:42+00&quot;<br />&quot;1892-05-01 11:41:07+00:17:30&quot;</p><p>Cela semble lié à la gestion historique des timezone?<br /><a href="http://archives.postgresql.org/pgsql-general/2007-02/msg01132.php" rel="nofollow">http://archives.postgresql.org/pgsql-ge … g01132.php</a></p><p>Je vais probablement passer ma colonne au format &quot;timestamp without timezone&quot;...</p>]]></content>
